# Speaker biometrics. The glob matters: voiceprint.json was ignored but voiceprint.json.bak
# was not, so a re-enrolment backup of the owner's voice embeddings sat untracked-but-committable.
voiceprint.json*
# FACE biometrics (37.R4, found 2026-09-20). The voiceprint got a named rule after that near-miss;
# face data never got the equivalent one, and was covered only incidentally - the single copy on
# this host happens to sit under the already-ignored backups/. A face embedding landing anywhere
# else in the tree had nothing stopping it. Owner face data never leaves the laptop, so it gets a
# rule of its own rather than relying on where a backup script chose to put it.
owner.npy
*.npy
faces/
runtime_prefs.json
mushegh_session.json
mushegh_tasks.sqlite
